 "atrNamesInvoice": {
  "about": "atrNamesInvoice over ATR bytes written by hand from A_N. N is L6.invoice and N2 is plant2.invoice; expect maps each to atrNamesInvoice(bytes, invoice). members is the object's member names in the order written, duplicates kept, as Python 3 json.loads with object_pairs_hook lists them; it is null where the bytes begin with a byte-order mark, which RFC 8259 section 8.1 forbids a writer to add and the core never writes. The ATR names an invoice only when its first members are atrVersion, id and x402 in the core's order and no member name repeats (RFC 8259 section 4: names within an object should be unique, and readers differ on repeated names), so every reader finds the one x402 member.",
